WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:01.872
(soft acoustic music)

00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:06.176
- [Voiceover] This is
Sade, and this is Linah,

00:00:06.176 --> 00:00:07.676
two young servals.

00:00:09.272 --> 00:00:11.447
These slender, medium size cats

00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:13.742
are native to sub-Saharan Africa,

00:00:13.742 --> 00:00:17.482
and have a gorgeous golden
coat with black spots.

00:00:17.482 --> 00:00:19.671
Servals have the longest legs

00:00:19.671 --> 00:00:22.769
of any cat relative to body size.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:25.356
Their ears are also impressively large,

00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:28.287
and can rotate 180 degrees,

00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:30.316
giving them a keen sense of hearing,

00:00:30.316 --> 00:00:33.281
which helps them locate prey efficiently.

00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:37.318
They're long, lean, and can
jump up to nine feet in the air,

00:00:37.318 --> 00:00:40.872
to catch unsuspecting birds flying by.

00:00:40.872 --> 00:00:43.723
Beyond birds, they mostly feed on rodents,

00:00:43.723 --> 00:00:45.473
insects and reptiles.

00:00:46.573 --> 00:00:48.803
Servals prefer wetlands and areas

00:00:48.803 --> 00:00:51.728
with tall grasses near water.

00:00:51.728 --> 00:00:54.627
Unfortunately, degradation
of these wetlands

00:00:54.627 --> 00:00:57.447
is leaving them with less and less space,

00:00:57.447 --> 00:00:59.715
while hunting for their prized coat

00:00:59.715 --> 00:01:02.024
remains a big concern.

00:01:02.024 --> 00:01:03.607
This is the serval.

